flag(7,'distractors','All three wrong mappings mostly pair representations with unrelated algorithm scores/settings. Use permutations of the same three actual representation classes, with parallel detail.')
flag(10,'distractors','The wrong options assert no evaluation, uniform probabilities regardless of fitness, or every child reproducing one seed. None seriously contrasts diversity with plausible exploitation/initialization tradeoffs.')
flag(12,'calculations explanation','The o1 rationale does not generate C=32. Applying weight 10 to the two turns as well as to the obstacle gives 12+10+20=42, not 32. Explain the actual alternate computation or revise the alternate value coherently.')
flag(13,'sourceSupport','The formula record includes C=L+alpha*N_obs+beta*N_turn although only p1311, the inverse transform, is cited. Narrow the record to the tested F(C) law or add p1310 as the cost-law premise.')
flag(14,'distractors','o3 claims N_turn must equal N_obs, an unrelated and implausible reason that the routes cannot be scored. Replace it with a coherent but mistaken penalty/ranking calculation.')
flag(27,'explanation difficulty duplication','o1 is not uniformly a first-gene swap: its first pair is the unchanged P6/P4 parents in reversed order, while its second pair does swap first genes. The rationale must describe both accurately. Two repetitions of Q026 whole-gene swapping do not justify medium difficulty or a new unique concept; mark as an easy variant or replace with the integrated generation angle below.')
flag(34,'distractors','The alternatives claim all parent collisions are preserved or one good mutation must be applied to every child. Use credible competing causal interpretations of C1-prime and C2 rather than absolute rules contradicted immediately by the stem.')
flag(35,'distractors','o1 explicitly claims 44 is greater than 44, allowing rejection without any GA knowledge. Replace with a numerically coherent comparison or inheritance misconception.')
flag(36,'distractors','o3 scores chromosome IDs and o4 uses scores of children before they exist. Replace these with plausible evaluation-order, stale-score or repair-timing alternatives.')
flag(37,'distractors','Lexicographic coordinate order as fitness (o3) is not a plausible final-score repair. Keep alternatives focused on when and which population is evaluated, or how an evaluated elite is returned.')
flag(39,'distractors','o1 assigns maximum fitness from free points and o2 deletes the goal. Neither is a credible repair/re-evaluation policy. Contrast waypoint-only validation, segment rechecking and score invalidation.')
flag(41,'distractors','o4 moves theta1 to C and theta2 to A rather than offering a plausible angular reference convention. Contrast absolute vertical, absolute horizontal, relative joint and signed-angle conventions.')
flag(44,'distractors','The friction-loss explanation o1 is unrelated to the stated frictionless gravity model. Replace with a plausible center-of-mass projection or frame-origin error.')
flag(45,'calculations explanation sourceSupport','The o3 rationale says placing both weights at full-link distances yields cosine coefficients 4 and 4. Including translation of W2 with bar 1 instead yields 8 and 4; coefficients 4 and 4 also omit that translation. Describe both mistakes or revise the option. The extra F=-Pi-7 formula is not supported by sole p1327 citation; remove the irrelevant shift or cite p1330.')
flag(46,'sourceSupport','The attached energy formula record also introduces F=-Pi-7, which is absent from cited pp1327/1328. Narrow the record to the energy/gradient being tested or cite p1330 for the additional shift.')
flag(47,'sourceSupport','The solution expressly corrects the derivative using the actual p1327 potential, but only the conflicting derivative page1328 is cited. Add p1327 as the premise for that correction, including the concept source map.')
flag(50,'sourceSupport','The irrelevant attached F=-Pi-7 transformation is absent from cited pp1327/1328. Remove it from the Hessian formula context or cite p1330 for it.')
flag(55,'distractors','o2 makes every visibly separated point the same minimum, and o4 introduces map obstacles into an angle-energy plot. Use plausible permutations of the actual selected/rejected/minimum marker categories.')
flag(57,'sourceSupport','The conclusion about roulette weights uses the p_i=F_i/sum(F) rule, but only the energy pages1327/1330 are cited. Add p1319 as the selection premise and avoid unrelated expected-copy formula material unless needed.')
flag(58,'sourceSupport difficulty','The formula record decodes four-bit substrings but omits p1329, where the inclusive mapping is actually defined. Cite it or remove the unnecessary decoder formula because angles are already supplied. With those angles supplied this is a direct formula substitution, so easy is better calibrated than medium.')
flag(60,'sourceSupport','The shift-versus-probability conclusion and attached roulette formula need p1319 as a source premise. Pages1330/1331 give the shifted energy and population but not normalized roulette probabilities.')
flag(63,'distractors','All wrong choices rely on extreme unrelated claims: graph search ignores costs/obstacles, one GA generation certifies optimality, or GAs cannot encode shortest paths. Use realistic known-graph versus irregular/multiobjective task tradeoffs.')
flag(64,'distractors','o3 changes the task to sensor calibration and o4 discards the goal and uses PRM for current control. Use parallel, plausible assignments of seeding, waypoint optimization and path tracking.')
flag(65,'distractors explanation','o4 describes a compensating action but falsely says it worsens the imbalance: after L becomes 100L, multiplying all other cost terms by 100 makes the whole objective 100 times the original and restores its rankings. The key remains uniquely true only because o4 appends a false consequence; its rationale does not explain this. Rewrite a coherent wrong scaling action and use a plausible alternative instead of removing collision checks in o3.')
flag(66,'distractors','All wrong options claim plots replace collision checks, prove global optimality, or establish stability. Use credible alternative diagnostics/interpretations, such as best versus population mean, genotype versus phenotype diversity, and visual stagnation.')
flag(67,'distractors','o1 adds stored scalar count to obstacle count as path length, an implausible metric. Replace with a realistic waypoint-boundary, signed-increment or backtracking mistake.')
flag(70,'distractors','o1 deliberately removes diversity and o3 stops cost checking after identical chromosomes. Contrast plausible adjustments in selection pressure, elite fraction and mutation strength without obvious abandonment of the algorithm.')
